volunteers are working to help raise  funds to rescue golden retrievers out of  china and the next step is to get all  those dogs to loving homes right here in  southern nevada we caught up with the  committee chair of goldens without  borders who lives in henderson about the  challenges this particular rescue group  is dealing with during this pandemic  it just means a lot to me to say that  margot rogat is a dog lover is an  understatement  this is one of the happiest moments for  her greeting these pups at lax it means  she saved a golden retriever headed to  the slaughterhouse in china or from a  life spent in a cage  margo's basically the head honcho  volunteer at goldens without borders  it's an international rescue that has in  the past relied on passenger flights to  transport these dogs from china to lax  and then drive them safely home to las  vegas but due to coveted restrictions  it's much more complicated and expensive  now we have an unbelievable rescue  partner in china and we arranged for all  the flights and everything to come into  the states have changed dramatically  since cobit and i do need dramatically  because now the dogs can only be  transported as cargo and the cost to do  so has more than quadrupled as a result  volunteers fundraise to cover the cost  and prepare all the necessary paperwork  for travel permits to the u.s oversea  rescue partners provide a safe  environment and prepare the dogs for  travel which includes vaccinations and  quarantine there's just a lot of dogs  that still need to come over here she  says it's rewarding work when you see  these dogs experience their first taste  of freedom  from where they've come and from the  life that they've known  which is not a life  and for many of them  it doesn't really become a life because  we can't save them all  but for the ones that we do  their lives are changed forever these  dogs are living  such a long life i mean  just  going to the beach or going to the snow  or kayaking or boating or lounging in a  swimming pool  there you go  and once they get here to las vegas  they're placed in foster families and  then they get the process to actually  adopt so it takes a little bit but  there's so many ways to get involved you  know that's such a great cause and  golden retrievers who doesn't want a  golden retriever they know they're such  lovely lovely dogs and of course there  are so many rescue organizations across  the country for so many different breeds  this happens to be for those now there  is a big fundraiser coming up in one  week it's called life is golden it's  taking place next thursday august 19th  at 5 30 at dragon ridge country club at  mcdonald highlands if you can't make the  event though and you just want to donate  to the cause you can do so at goldens  without borders dot org
 

